    <briefdescription>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Bidirectional edge value iterator.</para><para>Iterates over the edge values in a list, returning the user-defined value (type <ref refid="classSawyer_1_1Container_1_1Graph_1a01453c8fabdf45adf07e5319c2d46c43" kindref="member">EdgeValue</ref>) when dereferenced. <ref refid="classSawyer_1_1Container_1_1Graph_1_1Edge" kindref="compound">Edge</ref> iterators are stable across insert and erase operations. The difference between <ref refid="classSawyer_1_1Container_1_1Graph_1_1EdgeValueIterator" kindref="compound">EdgeValueIterator</ref> and <ref refid="classSawyer_1_1Container_1_1Graph_1_1ConstEdgeValueIterator" kindref="compound">ConstEdgeValueIterator</ref> is that the latter returns const references when dereferenced. </para>    </detaileddescription>
